WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.408
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.708 --> 00:00:09.385
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.685 --> 00:00:15.878
Unit twenty-four: Articles in Depth. Today you will use a, an, the and the zero article correctly.

4
00:00:16.178 --> 00:00:18.958
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.214
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:24.830
A.

7
00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:29.105
A means used before a consonant sound; first mention.

8
00:00:29.717 --> 00:00:30.985
A teacher came.

9
00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:34.352
Your turn. Say: A.

10
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:37.946
A.

11
00:00:38.683 --> 00:00:39.406
An.

12
00:00:40.417 --> 00:00:42.579
An means used before a vowel sound.

13
00:00:43.183 --> 00:00:44.150
An apple.

14
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.938
Your turn. Say: An.

15
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:50.372
An.

16
00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:51.804
The.

17
00:00:52.817 --> 00:00:55.315
The means used for something specific or known.

18
00:00:55.917 --> 00:00:57.324
The teacher is kind.

19
00:00:57.917 --> 00:01:00.337
Your turn. Say: The.

20
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:03.853
The.

21
00:01:04.617 --> 00:01:05.862
Zero article.

22
00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:09.569
Zero article means no article is used.

23
00:01:10.183 --> 00:01:11.370
I like music.

24
00:01:11.983 --> 00:01:14.891
Your turn. Say: Zero article.

25
00:01:17.733 --> 00:01:19.222
Zero article.

26
00:01:19.983 --> 00:01:20.857
General.

27
00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:23.942
General means about things in general.

28
00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:25.725
Dogs are loyal.

29
00:01:26.317 --> 00:01:29.004
Your turn. Say: General.

30
00:01:31.867 --> 00:01:32.763
General.

31
00:01:33.517 --> 00:01:34.657
Specific.

32
00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:38.520
Specific means a particular person or thing.

33
00:01:39.117 --> 00:01:40.454
The dog next door.

34
00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.702
Your turn. Say: Specific.

35
00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:47.579
Specific.

36
00:01:48.317 --> 00:01:49.109
Unique.

37
00:01:50.117 --> 00:01:52.314
Unique means only one of its kind.

38
00:01:52.917 --> 00:01:54.196
The sun is unique.

39
00:01:54.783 --> 00:01:57.134
Your turn. Say: Unique.

40
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.955
Unique.

41
00:02:01.717 --> 00:02:02.776
Countries.

42
00:02:03.783 --> 00:02:05.469
Countries means nations.

43
00:02:06.083 --> 00:02:07.630
Cambodia is a country.

44
00:02:08.217 --> 00:02:10.706
Your turn. Say: Countries.

45
00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:14.579
Countries.

46
00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:19.215
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:23.303
Visal, why do we say the Mekong but just Cambodia?

48
00:02:24.417 --> 00:02:40.827
Rivers, oceans, mountain ranges and countries with plural or union names take the: the Mekong, the Pacific, the United States. Most single countries and cities use no article: Cambodia, Phnom Penh.

49
00:02:41.917 --> 00:02:43.289
When do we use a and the?

50
00:02:44.383 --> 00:02:58.973
A or an for the first mention or one of many: I saw a dog. The for the second mention or something unique or known: The dog was big. The sun, the moon, the government.

51
00:03:00.083 --> 00:03:01.862
When do we use no article?

52
00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:18.880
With general plurals and uncountable nouns: I like music. Dogs are loyal. Also with meals and languages: I have breakfast at seven. We speak Khmer. Remember an before a vowel sound.

53
00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.603
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:26.864
Grammar focus: Articles: a and an and the and zero.

55
00:03:27.164 --> 00:03:28.305
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:29.017 --> 00:03:31.553
I saw a dog. The dog was big.

57
00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.624
We sail on the Mekong in Cambodia.

58
00:03:35.517 --> 00:03:37.191
I like music (no article).

59
00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:46.140
A / an for first mention. The for known or unique things and rivers. No article for general plurals, uncountable nouns and most countries.

60
00:03:46.883 --> 00:03:50.209
Be careful! Don't say: He lives in the Cambodia.

61
00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:54.317
Say: He lives in Cambodia.

62
00:03:54.617 --> 00:03:56.756
No article for most countries.

63
00:03:57.567 --> 00:04:00.289
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:02.542
A, An, The or Nothing?.

65
00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:05.271
I saw a dog and an elephant at the zoo.

66
00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:08.603
The dog was big, and the elephant was bigger.

67
00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.820
We live in Cambodia, near the Mekong.

68
00:04:12.833 --> 00:04:15.611
I like music, and I have breakfast at seven.

69
00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:18.507
The sun is unique in our sky.

70
00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:23.323
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:24.183 --> 00:04:26.299
I saw blank elephant yesterday.

72
00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:29.161
A, a. B, an. C, the.

73
00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.282
The answer is B: an.

74
00:04:35.417 --> 00:04:37.497
blank Mekong is a long river.

75
00:04:37.797 --> 00:04:41.114
A, A. B, The. C, No article.

76
00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.144
The answer is B: The.

77
00:04:47.283 --> 00:04:48.877
I like blank music.

78
00:04:49.177 --> 00:04:52.319
A, the. B, a. C, no article.

79
00:04:55.867 --> 00:04:58.110
The answer is C: no article.

80
00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.308
Which uses the correct article?

81
00:05:01.608 --> 00:05:07.792
A, He lives in the Cambodia.. B, He lives in Cambodia.. C, He lives in a Cambodia..

82
00:05:11.333 --> 00:05:13.797
The answer is B: He lives in Cambodia..

83
00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.170
According to the reading, what is unique?

84
00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:21.124
A, the sun. B, a dog. C, music.

85
00:05:24.667 --> 00:05:26.666
The answer is A: the sun.

86
00:05:27.867 --> 00:05:31.158
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:32.017 --> 00:05:34.608
Why do we say 'the Mekong' but just 'Cambodia'?

88
00:05:43.417 --> 00:05:44.963
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:45.263 --> 00:05:59.052
We say the Mekong because rivers take the. We say Cambodia without an article because most single countries do not use one. Articles depend on the kind of noun and whether it is specific.

90
00:05:59.352 --> 00:06:01.050
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:07.354
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and articles: a and an and the and zero.

92
00:06:07.654 --> 00:06:11.723
Today's value is precision. Choose your words and numbers with care.

93
00:06:12.023 --> 00:06:14.896
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

94
00:06:15.196 --> 00:06:18.533
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

